Sass (SCSS) Installation & Setup Guide
======================================

This guide outlines the steps to install and configure Sass for the project.
The process uses npm to install Dart Sass as a development dependency.

1. Project Setup
----------------
If package.json does not exist:
   npm init -y

Install the Sass compiler:
   npm install sass --save-dev

2. Directory Structure
----------------------
Ensure the file structure follows this pattern:

project/
|-- src/
|   |-- styles/
|   |   |-- main.scss    (Sass source code INPUT)
|-- dist/
|   |-- css/
|   |   |-- main.css     (Compiled CSS OUTPUT)

3. NPM Script Configuration
---------------------------
Add the following 'sass' script to the "scripts" section in the package.json:

"scripts": {
  "sass": "sass src/styles/main.scss dist/css/main.css --watch"
}

4. Running Sass
---------------

A. Development Mode (Continuous Watch)
   Use this command during development to automatically compile CSS on every save.
   The terminal must remain open while running.

   npm run sass

B. Production Build (Minified)
   Use this command to create a compressed, final version of the CSS for deployment.
   This runs once and exits.

   sass src/styles/main.scss dist/css/main.min.css --style=compressed

5. HTML Integration
-------------------
Always link to the compiled CSS output file (not the SCSS source) in the HTML:

<link rel="stylesheet" href="dist/css/main.css" />


Notes
-----
- The 'dist/css' directory is generated output and should not be modified manually.
- SCSS features (variables, nesting, mixins) are fully supported.
- Sass files starting with an underscore (e.g., _partial.scss) are considered partials and are not compiled on their own.
